  "body": "The `HTMLImageElement` interface has two attributes [`naturalWidth`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#dom-img-naturalwidth) and [`naturalHeight`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#dom-img-naturalheight), which return the density-corrected intrinsic width and height of the image.\r\n\r\nThough there is no way to get the dimensions of an image loaded via a `<picture>` element. Therefore those two attributes should get added to the [`HTMLPictureElement`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#htmlpictureelement) as well.\r\n\r\nSebastian",
